OL,3,GNEWSA#1m towards fighting city child
OL,4,Apoverty 'crisis'
OL,5,
OL,6,FCity leaders are to commit more than
OL,7,F#1m towards a programme to tackle
OL,8,F"crisis levels" of child poverty.
OL,10,FA report to Liverpool City Council
OL,11,Fwarns 40% of children in the city are
OL,12,Fliving in poverty - the highest rate in
OL,13,FMerseyside.
OL,15,FThese youngsters are typically up to 19
OL,16,Fmonths behind their peers in language
OL,17,Fand communication by the time they
OL,18,Fstart school, it warns.
